Translation patch: `ComStmtBulkExecuteRequest(Builder)` and `StmtBulkExecuteParamValues`

Change:
  - `add_row`: `self.arity.get_or_insert(params.len())` becomes a `match` that stores `Some(params.len())` when `None`; `for p in &params` becomes an index loop.
  - `build`: `mem::take(&mut self.params_set)` becomes `mem::replace(&mut self.params_set, Vec::new())`.
  - `StmtBulkExecuteParamValues`: `for param in params` (a `Vec` of `Copy` pairs) and `for value in &self.values` become index loops.
  - `ComStmtBulkExecuteRequest::new`: `values.first().ok_or(NoParams)?` becomes `if values.is_empty() { return Err(NoParams) }` and `values[0]`; the two `iter().map(from_value).collect()` become a helper `bulk_param_types(row)` (index loop); `for values in &values` becomes an index loop; the inner `for (left, right) in types.iter_mut().zip(&row_types)` moves into a helper `merge_bulk_param_types(&mut types, &row_types)` looping over the shorter length, with `left != right` written as `left.column_type() != right.column_type() || left.flags() != right.flags()`; `StmtBulkExecuteParamValues::new(values.into_iter().flatten())` becomes `StmtBulkExecuteParamValues { values: take_bulk_param_values(&mut values) }`, which moves each value out with `mem::replace(.., Value::NULL)` in row-major order (helper `take_bulk_param_row`) and wraps it with `StmtBulkExecuteParamValue::new`; `Vec::default()` becomes `Vec::new()`.
  - `MyDeserialize`: the `zip` loop over the parsed types and `params` moves into a helper `set_bulk_param_types(&types, &mut params)` (index loop over the shorter length); `Seq::empty()` becomes `Seq::new(Vec::new())`.
  - `MySerialize`: `if contains(SEND_TYPES_TO_SERVER) { types.serialize } values.serialize` becomes `if .. { types.serialize; values.serialize } else { values.serialize }`.
Why: Aeneas does not model iterator adaptors (`map`/`collect`/`zip`/`flatten`/`iter_mut`), the `Vec` and slice iterators, `get_or_insert`, `first`, `mem::take` or `Default for Vec`; it fails on `Seq::empty`'s promoted `&[]` constant, on nested `values[i][j]` indexing, and on the join after the `if` in `serialize`.
Behaviour: Identical results: the same elements in the same order, with the same early returns. `zip` stops at the shorter sequence. The derived `PartialEq` of `StmtBulkExecuteParamType` compares its two `Const` fields, i.e. the column type and the flags. `mem::take` is `mem::replace` with `Default::default()`, which is `Vec::new()`. `values` is not used after the values are moved out of it (it is dropped). Only the representation of the empty `types` changes, from `Cow::Borrowed(&[])` to `Cow::Owned(vec![])`; `Seq` compares, hashes, dereferences and serializes by contents, so this is not observable through its API. (`add_params`, `build_params_iter`, `build_iter`, which take `Params` or iterators, and `StmtBulkExecuteParamValues::new` are not translated.)

